Input validation steps
----------------------
1. add the maven dependency

<dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
    </dependency>

2. use the validation annotations
3. use @Valid along with @RequestBody
4. test the endpoints which check for input validations


exception handling in 3 ways
----------------------------
1. conventional try... catch
2. using @ExceptionHandler at each controller level
3. global exception handlers --- preferred one
	1. create a class and annotate it with @RestControllerAdvice
	2. create methods and annotate it with @ExceptionHandler and specify the exception to be handled
	3. within the method return ResponseEntity object with the exception message that u want return back



Spring Data JPA steps
----------------------
1. Add the spring data jpa dependency in pom.xml
	Spring web - for spring rest
	spring data jpa - for Spring data jpa
	Lombok
	validation - input validation
	MySQL driver - db driver
2. make entry in application.properties file

	# Database Connection Settings
	spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/mms_db
	spring.datasource.username=root
	spring.datasource.password=root
	spring.datasource.driver-class-name=com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver

	# JPA / Hibernate Properties
	#spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
	spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=validate
	spring.jpa.show-sql=true

3. create the table on the database side
4. create the necessary packages in your project
5. create the Entity class and map it to the table in the DB
6. finish dao layer
7. finish service layer
8. finish controller layer
9. test the endpoints
